{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T15:59:08.400Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1781","claim:pm-gh1787","claim:pm-glmcnd","claim:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-gh1787","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1781+pm-gh1787+pm-glmcnd+pm-jzrtsr","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1781","claim:pm-gh1787","claim:pm-glmcnd","claim:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-gh1787","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-26T15:59:08.399Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 1 on PR #1789, both P2 findings confirmed against git rev-parse and fixed. (1) A link start directory: Git walks the physical ancestors, so with root/wslink -> parent/ws/child2 and ceiling parent/ws Git finds no repository, while the logical walk reached parent. Discovery now walks physical ancestors and maps the result back to the caller's spelling where a logical ancestor resolves to it, else reports the physical path. (2) Ignored entries became active: before the first empty entry an entry Git cannot resolve (parent/missing/..) is dropped, and after it an entry is compared as spelled with one trailing separator trimmed, so child/.. is inert. Seven unit cases now, three of which fail on the previous implementation."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T15:59:08.400Z"}],"before_hash":"03a95f8e3451d246aaea6ed96e4a4d4278c3d2dfb753d10887f7b8608686bceb","after_hash":"753314f09f49f75f6bc705425437c501a779daf992715a30eba84e24d63605cb","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"f9952e4a1dd9db5108e53556c7a54d1814255ad1890d1a8bd2d5d710c7865c9f"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T16:52:10.815Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1781","claim:pm-gh1787","claim:pm-glmcnd","claim:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-gh1787","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1781+pm-gh1787+pm-glmcnd+pm-jzrtsr","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1781","claim:pm-gh1787","claim:pm-glmcnd","claim:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-gh1787","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-26T16:52:10.814Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 2 on PR #1789: three discovery findings confirmed with git and fixed. A start spelled through a link and then dot-dot now resolves as spelled before normalization, as chdir does; one discovery now decides both coordinates, with no rediscovery from a normalized fallback; pm_root_rel is computed between physical paths when both sides resolve, so a source reached through a link alias keeps its tracker-relative path. Only the platform's own separators are trimmed after an empty ceiling entry, so a trailing backslash on POSIX names another directory as Git reads it. Round 2 adds four unit cases; three fail on the previous implementation."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T16:52:10.815Z"}],"before_hash":"753314f09f49f75f6bc705425437c501a779daf992715a30eba84e24d63605cb","after_hash":"8acfd145c2df4b61752869e2f3a25f91881294689a4d5547758c7182d3690218","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"452df3b167b739475893d9d622ac0ac555f8bdaa823ee5b96a5c04f064b7e7d1"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T17:05:59.840Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1781","claim:pm-gh1787","claim:pm-glmcnd","claim:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-gh1787","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1781+pm-gh1787+pm-glmcnd+pm-jzrtsr","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1781","claim:pm-gh1787","claim:pm-glmcnd","claim:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-gh1787","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-26T17:05:59.839Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 3 on PR #1789: without a checkout, the source root was the normalized spelling of the start (link/.. collapsed lexically), not the directory the walk started from, so a tracker could be classified as contained in a directory discovery never examined. discoverSourceWorkspace now returns the source and the checkout from one walk; without a checkout the source is the physical start unless the caller's spelling names the same directory."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T17:05:59.840Z"}],"before_hash":"8acfd145c2df4b61752869e2f3a25f91881294689a4d5547758c7182d3690218","after_hash":"7c0c8b2543870fc12e970d7e178dd8f93137d5a6e15e1057f35d31a07577ef7f","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"be589b4603bc2dd93c963655baad6ab7b888b4ac788fbafcc5a8dc89d3df228c"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T17:16:20.718Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"bde5973a64851be416b1c911","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1781","claim:pm-gh1787","claim:pm-glmcnd","claim:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-gh1787","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1781+pm-gh1787+pm-glmcnd+pm-jzrtsr","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1781","claim:pm-gh1787","claim:pm-glmcnd","claim:pm-jzrtsr","lineage:pm-gh1787","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-26T17:16:20.718Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 4 on PR #1789, recorded residual: before the first empty entry Git resolves a ceiling component by component and accepts a regular-file component followed by .. (README.md/.. names its directory), while realpathSync.native rejects it with ENOTDIR, so such an entry is dropped instead of becoming a ceiling. Replicating Git's resolver for a ceiling spelled through a file is out of proportion; a ceiling that names a directory behaves as Git's. CodeRabbit: an entry after an empty one is now compared in the walk's native separator form (Git for Windows writes C:/parent)."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T17:16:20.718Z"}],"before_hash":"7c0c8b2543870fc12e970d7e178dd8f93137d5a6e15e1057f35d31a07577ef7f","after_hash":"3765efc7c6e29c65bd4a7126fe7fbc0c4967613712b2995c434339343844d858","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_